speakersafetyd: speakersafetyd (Apple Silicon speaker protection daemon)
speakersafetyd:
speakersafetyd: Enforces thermal limits on Apple Silicon speakers,
speakersafetyd: which can be driven beyond what they survive. Asahi's kernel
speakersafetyd: driver holds them at a reduced volume until this daemon runs;
speakersafetyd: the daemon then lifts that limit while it monitors them.
speakersafetyd:
speakersafetyd: Upstream relies on systemd; this package wires it into the
speakersafetyd: SysV boot via /etc/rc.d/rc.speakersafetyd instead.
speakersafetyd: REQUIRED: without it Asahi's driver keeps the speakers quiet.
speakersafetyd: Homepage: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/speakersafetyd
